        <p>Colombo is Sri Lanka's commercial capital and the arrival point for most international visitors, but few people stay long — the city's real value is as a launchpad. Within two to three hours of the city centre you can reach ancient kingdoms, UNESCO World Heritage Sites, elephant orphanages, colonial-era beach towns, spectacular rock fortresses, and one of the finest wildlife parks in Asia. If you have a day or two between flights, or want to see Sri Lanka's highlights without building a full itinerary, these are the best day trips from Colombo.</p>

